<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso I of Aragon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso I of Aragon, known as the Battler, was king of Aragon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> in the early twelfth century. He captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> in 1118 and won other territories from Muslim rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley. His conquests marked significant losses for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Alfonso I of Aragon" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willtron · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dinero_chaqu%C3%A9s_cara_Alifonso_I.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
